  "Project": {
    "Brief history of your project and organization": "We are building the next-generation decentralized IoT platform—one where data owners can fully realize the value of their data.\n\nAnyLog achieves this through proprietary technology that overcomes the core challenges of IoT data management: Volume, Velocity, and Variety. It enables existing applications to immediately access and act on all available IoT data, while unlocking entirely new applications that were previously impractical or impossible.\n\nUsing a globally distributed peer-to-peer network, blockchain-based coordination, an incentive layer, and massive parallelism, AnyLog offers a cost-effective and scalable solution for collecting, storing, and querying IoT data using standard SQL.\n\nWhat sets AnyLog apart from traditional SQL-based systems is its ability to execute SQL queries on distributed data without physically centralizing that data. When a query is issued, AnyLog automatically decomposes it into sub-queries, distributes them across relevant nodes, executes them locally, and returns a unified result set—delivering the experience of querying a single, centralized database while preserving decentralization.\n\nThe AnyLog network provides a simple, repeatable framework for managing IoT data, scales horizontally to accommodate massive datasets, and creates new opportunities to securely share and monetize data in a trusted, decentralized environment.",
    "Is this project associated with other projects/ecosystem stakeholders?": "Yes",
    "Describe the data being stored onto Filecoin": "As part of the AnyLog protocol, telemetry data is stored twice: once as files on the node’s local filesystem and once in a database. We plan to transition the file storage from the local filesystem to Filecoin. These files—often in JSON.",
